{"availability":"available","full":"qiangli/bashy","name":"bashy","description":"A pure-Go Bash 5.3 for Linux, macOS and Windows that also speaks Bash# — typed Go in shell text, fenced-language islands, and agentic blocks with contracts. Passes Bash's own 5.3 suite (86/86).","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":5,"forks":1,"created":"2026-06-14T22:53:05Z","updated":"2026-10-03T06:03:51Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://github.com/qiangli/bashsharp-tour","topics":["agents","bash","bashsharp","coding-agents","golang","posix","shell","windows"],"demo":null,"color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","stars":5,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["bashy is one static binary — no CGo, no system bash — that is a drop-in Bash 5.3 on Linux, macOS and Windows: same flags, same script semantics, same $BASHVERSION, and it passes GNU Bash's own 5.3 test suite (every runnable fixture, 86/86). With --bashsharp the same binary speaks Bash#: the bash you already know, Go where you need types, any fenced language where you need a library, and agentic where you need a model — with contracts so a model's output is judged, never trusted.","Alpha (0.x). Bash 5.3 compatibility is stable; the Bash# dialect may still change before 1.0 through RFCs. Every number this project states names its corpus: docs/claims.md."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/qiangli/bashy/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fe64ef736b43454e03b3165982e8c0ef5e826717ea833de5a11aa7b6700d16e6","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:36:58.563Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"bashy is one static binary — no CGo, no system bash — that is a d